llvm-4.0.0 backport patch: a conditional branch's uses give no edge to the region's exit (PS4)

This patch CHANGES CODE GENERATION for a block that ends in a conditional
branch: the schedulers built on ScheduleDAGInstrs (the MachineScheduler and
the post-RA list scheduler btver2 enables) no longer hold the flag setter
against the exit node. r286544 (Matthias Braun, 2016-11-11,
"ScheduleDAGInstrs: Add condjump deps to addSchedBarrierDeps()",
llvm-project 325cd2c98ab6, D25140, first release LLVM 4.0) added the
branch's uses to ExitSU and rewrote macro fusion to walk ExitSU's
predecessors and set the fused edge's latency to zero; with it the post-RA
scheduler lifts `test eax, eax` above an independent store (`mov
[rbx+0x554], eax`), where 3.9.1 and the base keep the store first
(0x83fef0: the machine code is the same in both releases until that pass;
round 192B). This patch takes back both code hunks: addSchedBarrierDeps
gives ExitSU the uses of a call or barrier only, and macro fusion looks at
the units with no successors that write a register the branch reads. The
signature changes of the commit (createMacroFusionDAGMutation without TRI)
are kept; they do not change code. With this patch 0x83fef0, 0x1380640,
0x1380850 and 0x1496a80 compile to the base's bytes and no matched game row
changes (the module sweep of round 192B, repeated by the supervisor with
this unconditional form).

diff -ru a/lib/CodeGen/MachineScheduler.cpp b/lib/CodeGen/MachineScheduler.cpp
--- a/lib/CodeGen/MachineScheduler.cpp
+++ b/lib/CodeGen/MachineScheduler.cpp
@@ -1579,12 +1579,28 @@
   if (!Branch)
     return;
 
-  for (SDep &PredDep : ExitSU.Preds) {
-    if (PredDep.isWeak())
+  // PS4: the SUnits with no successors that write a register the branch
+  // reads, as before r286544; its walk over ExitSU's predecessors is not taken.
+  const TargetRegisterInfo &TRI = *DAG->TRI;
+  for (SUnit &SU : DAG->SUnits) {
+    // SUnits with successors can't be schedule in front of the ExitSU.
+    if (!SU.Succs.empty())
       continue;
-    SUnit &SU = *PredDep.getSUnit();
-    MachineInstr &Pred = *SU.getInstr();
-    if (!TII.shouldScheduleAdjacent(Pred, *Branch))
+    // We only care if the node writes to a register that the branch reads.
+    MachineInstr *Pred = SU.getInstr();
+    bool HasDataDep = false;
+    for (const MachineOperand &MO : Branch->uses()) {
+      if (!MO.isReg() || !MO.readsReg())
+        continue;
+      if (Pred->modifiesRegister(MO.getReg(), &TRI)) {
+        HasDataDep = true;
+        break;
+      }
+    }
+    if (!HasDataDep)
+      continue;
+
+    if (!TII.shouldScheduleAdjacent(*Pred, *Branch))
       continue;
 
     // Create a single weak edge from SU to ExitSU. The only effect is to cause
@@ -1597,16 +1613,8 @@
     (void)Success;
     assert(Success && "No DAG nodes should be reachable from ExitSU");
 
-    // Adjust latency of data deps between the nodes.
-    for (SDep &PredDep : ExitSU.Preds) {
-      if (PredDep.getSUnit() == &SU)
-        PredDep.setLatency(0);
-    }
-    for (SDep &SuccDep : SU.Succs) {
-      if (SuccDep.getSUnit() == &ExitSU)
-        SuccDep.setLatency(0);
-    }
-
+    // PS4: no latency set to zero between the fused nodes, as before r286544;
+    // its latency adjustment is not taken.
     DEBUG(dbgs() << "Macro Fuse SU(" << SU.NodeNum << ")\n");
     break;
   }
